# The conan recipe revision is a hash of the EXPORTED files -- conanfile.py,
# buildutil.toml, CMakeLists.txt and the whole sources/ tree (the recipe's
# exports/exports_sources). A CRLF checkout on the Windows publish runner
# would hash differently from the Linux and macOS lanes, splitting one
# release across two recipe revisions: consumers resolve the LATEST revision
# and would find only the binaries published under it. Force LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# a patch context line must match the pinned tree byte for byte, and that
# tree is CRLF
*.patch -text
